    "https://www.unisg.ch/en/studying/why-hsg/great-career-opportunities/": {
      "title": "Great Career Opportunities",
      "description": "HSG - Uni SG - Great career opportunities Privacy settings We use cookies/targeting and process personal data to measure results and/or tailor the content of our website. Because we value your privacy, we ask for your permission. You can change/adjust your consent at any time in the \"Privacy settings\". Accept all cookies Accept required cookies Settings Data Protection Declaration Copyright & Disclaimer Privacy settings × Required cookies TYPO3 Consent Management Solution Functional cookies and pixels Google Analytics Crazy Egg Marketing cookies and pixels LinkedIn Meta Pixel Google Ads / Google Marketing Platform TikTok Pinterest Reddit Application related cookies Vimeo Youtube iFrame Other Applications Google Maps Required cookies This concerns: this consent menu incl. proof of consent TYPO3-Session Cookie (file transferred to the user's computer). Cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be deactivated. However, you can set your browser to block these cookies or to notify you of these cookies. However, some areas of the website will then not function or only function to a limited extent. For further information, please refer to the HSG data protection declaration of the: HSG – Website HSG – Your information request and voluntary contributions TYPO3 TYPO3 uses so-called session cookies (\"cookies\") by default. A TYPO3 cookie is a small data file that is transferred to the visitor's computer, but cannot identify the visitor personally. It only stores the browser installed on the visitor's computer, the visitor's activities, and the user's name and e-mail address when the user fills out a comment form. Consent Management Solution When you visit the website, \"cookies\" may be installed on your computer's hard drive for the sole purpose of making the website more responsive to the needs of returning visitors. These mini-files or cookies are not used to monitor the visitor's browsing behaviour on other websites. Internet browsers allow you to block the use of cookies. You will receive a warning when a cookie is installed or a notification that the cookies can then be removed from your hard drive. Please refer to the help function of your internet browser. Functional cookies and pixels These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They are set by third-party providers whose services the HSG uses on the pages of its domain. For further information, please refer to the HSG data protection declaration of the: HSG – Third Parties Google Analytics Google Analytics is a web analytics service provided by Alphabet Inc / Google LLC / Google Ireland Limited / Google Inc for the purpose of analysing how users use the website. Specifically: Reporting on website activity for the HSG Provision of other services associated with the use of the website and the Internet. After the cookie has been saved on your computer, personal data is collected: IP address / abbreviated IP address Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://policies.google.com/privacy Information on the third party can be found at: about.google Crazy Egg Crazy Egg is a website optimisation tool to obtain statistics about user behaviour on a website. Once the cookie is stored on your computer, it can help optimise the website for your use. In-formation is stored which provides information about where you have clicked: where you clicked how long you stayed on individual pages of the domain The following are transmitted to Crazy Egg: the first three bytes of your IP address the click coordinates other parameters provided by your web browser Information on data protection, retention period, storage locations and third parties can be found at: www.crazyegg.com/ Marketing cookies and pixels These cookies may be set by advertising partners. They may be used by these companies to profile your interests and show you relevant ads on other websites. This is based on a unique identification of your browser and internet device. For further information, please refer to the HSG data protection declaration of the: HSG – Third Parties LinkedIn It is used by LinkedIn Corporation: Conversion tracking technology Retargeting function This technology can be used to serve personalised ads on LinkedIn to users of this website. Furthermore, it is possible to create anonymous reports on the performance of the advertise-ments and information on website interaction. For this purpose, the LinkedIn In-Sight tag is integrated on this website, which establishes a connection to the LinkedIn server if you are logged into your LinkedIn account at the same time. Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://www.linkedin.com/legal/privacy-policy Information on the third party can be found at: https://www.linkedin.com Meta Pixel This is a tracking technology of Facebook Inc. / Facebook Ireland Limited, which is placed as a pixel in the browser and used for: Marketing Retargeting Tracking Analysis Advertising The following personal data is collected: Facebook user ID Browser information Usage data Non-sensitive custom data Referrer URL Pixel ID User behaviour Advertisements viewed Interactions with advertisements, services and products Marketing information Viewed content IP address Device information Marketing campaign success Geographical location Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://www.facebook.com/privacy/explanation Information on the third party can be found at: https://www.facebook.com Google Ads / Google Marketing Platform It is a service of Alphabet Inc. / Google LLC / Google Ireland Limited / Google Inc. for the pur pose of internet advertising, which allows advertisers to place ads in Google's search engine results as well as in the Google advertising network. The purpose of Google Ads / Google Marketing Platforms is the insertion of interest-relevant advertising on the websites of third-party companies and in the search engine results of the Google search engine, as well as the insertion of third-party advertising. A so-called conversion cookie is stored by Google in the information technology system of the data subject. In connection with AdWords and personal data, such as an IP address, Google: understands whether a data subject has completed or cancelled a purchase of goods compiles visit statistics determines the success or failure of AdWords ads and optimizes them Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://www.google.de/intl/de/policies/privacy/ Information on the third party can be found at: https://about.google/ TikTok This is a code from TikTok Information Technologies UK Limited which is implemented as a pixel on the website for the purpose of displaying targeted and personalised advertising to us-ers and to create interest-based user profiles. A connection is established to TikTok servers to collect the following personal data: IP address E-mail address Unit ID Device type Operating System In addition, behaviour on websites can be tracked, e.g. for measuring the effectiveness of ad placements. Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://www.tiktok.com/legal/page/eea/new-privacy-policy/en-EN Information on the third party can be found at: https://www.tiktok.com/ Pinterest Pinterest is a service provided by Pinterest Inc., USA, which is integrated into the website as a pixel, widget, or pin button for marketing and analysis purposes relating to users. A connection is established to Pinterest servers in order to collect the following personal data: Technical data: IP address Device information Browser information Operating system Screen resolution Language settings Usage data: Date/time of access Pages viewed Referrer URL (e.g., coming from Pinterest) Click behavior Cookie/tracking data: Unique Ids Session Ids Possibly hashed email address (if known) Location data (derived from IP or device information) Interaction data (content that is shared, pinned, or clicked on) Information on data protection, retention periods, and storage locations, including the US, can be found at: https://policy.pinterest.com/en/privacy-policy Reddit Functions of the Reddit platform are integrated into the website (the so-called Reddit Pixel). The provider is: Reddit Inc., 548 Market St #16093, San Francisco, CA 94104, USA. Reddit is a service provided by Reddit company, which is embedded as a pixel on the website of the University of St.Gallen. To optimise our content for your needs, personal and behavioural data are collected and processed in analytics tools such as Google Analytics, in particular: IP address Browser and device data Date and time of access Referrer URL (our website) Information about your use of embedded content Existing Reddit cookies or tracking IDs Reddit may use these data to provide embedded content, analyse user behaviour, display personalised content or advertising, and ensure the security of the platform. Further information about the purpose and scope of data collection by Reddit, the storage period and the storage locations in the United States can be found at: Reddit Privacy Policy Application related cookies These cookies are required by third party regulations when users voluntarily apply the relevant element. For further information, please refer to the HSG data protection declaration of the: HSG – Third Parties Vimeo This is a service provided by Vimeo LLC for the purpose of displaying video content. A cookie is placed in the browser and used to collect the following personal data: Browser information Browser language Browser type Cookie information Device information Device operating system Information from third party sources IP address Pages visited Referring URL Information users provide on the website Search queries Geographical location Retrieved content Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://vimeo.com/privacy Information on the third party can be found at: https://vimeo.com/ Youtube This is a service provided by Alphabet Inc. / Google LLC / Google Ireland Limited / Google Inc. for the purpose of displaying video content. A cookie is placed in the browser if the privacy-friendly mode is not activated and is used to collect the following personal data: Device information IP address Referring URL Retrieved videos Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=en Information on the third party can be found at: https://about.google/ iFrame Fremde Inhalte können per iFrame in der Seite integriert sein. Other Applications For further information, please refer to the HSG data protection declaration of the: HSG – Third Parties Google Maps This is an API (\"Application Programming Interface\") for the map service of Alphabet Inc. / Google LLC / Google Ireland Limited / Google Inc. for the purpose of an appealing presentation of the online offer and an easy findability of specified locations. When used, the IP address is collected as a personal data. No cookies are used. Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://www.google.com/intl/de_de/help/terms_maps/ Information on the third party can be found at: https://about.google/ Cancel Save and close path d=\"m521.23-480-123 123L440-314.23 605.77-480 440-645.77 398.23-603l123 123Zm-41.16 380q-78.84 0-148.21-29.92t-120.68-81.21q-51.31-51.29-81.25-120.63Q100-401.1 100-479.93q0-78.84 29.92-148.21t81.21-120.68q51.29-51.31 120.63-81.25Q401.1-860 479.93-860q78.84 0 148.21 29.92t120.68 81.21q51.31 51.29 81.25 120.63Q860-558.9 860-480.07q0 78.84-29.92 148.21t-81.21 120.68q-51.29 51.31-120.63 81.25Q558.9-100 480.07-100Zm-.07-60q134 0 227-93t93-227q0-134-93-227t-227-93q-134 0-227 93t-93 227q0 134 93 227t227 93Zm0-320Z\" fill=\"var(--color1, #000)\"/> Compose new email with × Gmail in browser Outlook in browser Yahoo in browser Default email app Copy Powered by MailtoUI Back search search close Studying Research Executive Education Transfer News University Kontakt en German English close Studying Overview Studying Overview Why HSG? Why HSG? Overview Engaged community Great career opportunities Superb study programmes HSG Best Talents Programmes Programmes Overview Bachelor Master Doctorate Exchange programmes Exchange programmes Overview Incoming Guest Students Outgoing HSG Students Get in touch Get in touch Overview Open Days & Exchanges Campus tours Fairs Offers for schools Services for businesses Admissions Admissions Overview Admission Bachelor Admission Master Admission Ph.D. Additional Qualification Programmes Recognition of degrees Application deadlines Rematriculation Studying at HSG Studying at HSG Overview Admitted – what's next? Semester dates Course choice and exams Costs of an HSG degree Living in St.Gallen Courses Orientation Orientation Overview Advice and support Campus Uni ABCs Research Overview Research Overview Research at HSG Research at HSG Overview Open Science Office Scientific Integrity & Research Ethics Research Support Research Services GSERM - Global School in Empirical Research Methods Prizes and Awards Faculty Faculty Overview Open Faculty Positions Faculty Portal Welcome Center Faculty Development Mid Career Programme Academic Career Development Research units Research units Overview Schools Institutes Global Centers Centers Strategic research collaboration Transparency Ph.D. Ph.D. Overview PhD Programme in Management (PMA) Graduate Programme in Economics and Finance (GPEF) Computer Science (DCS) Law (DLS) Organization Studies and Cultural Theory (DOK) International Affairs and Political Economy (DIA) Early Career Programme Research in Focus Research in Focus Overview Elite Quality Index Circular Lab Consumer Spending in Switzerland Alexandria Executive Education Overview Executive Education Overview Executive Programmes Board Programmes Custom Programmes Executive MBA MBA Educational Consultation Transfer Overview Transfer Overview Career & Corporate Services Career & Corporate Services Overview Einzelberatung Karriere-Workshops Werkzeuge und Vorlagen Stellenplattform HSG Entrepreneurship HSG Entrepreneurship Overview HSG Entrepreneurship Services Ideation Incubation Acceleration Community About us Teaching Research and Intellectual Property Insights and advice for partners from the world of work News Overview News Overview Newsroom Newsroom Overview Special Topic HSG Entrepreneurship Special Topic Artificial Intelligence Special Topic Sustainability Media releases Newsletter Events Events Overview Event calendar Öffentliche Vorlesungen Dies academicus HSG Graduation Days PhD Degree Award Ceremony St.Gallen Symposium START Summit Publications Publications Overview HSG Focus Brochures Research Platform Alexandria Video series Video series Overview Impact Awards In the Lab Knowledge Bank Art interviews Academic GIFts Little Green Bags Podcasts Podcasts Overview HSG Student Podcast Grüezi Amerika. Views from the Sister Republic Meet the CFO HSG Research Insight SQUARE Talks Innovations in Sustainable Finance Machines That Fail Us University Overview University Overview About us About us Overview Vision, strategy and values Organisation History Rankings and accreditations Quality development Art at the HSG Advisory offices HSG at a glance HSG at a glance Overview Numbers lab Research in focus The history of HSG Engagement Engagement Overview Student engagement Responsibility and Sustainability Diversity & Inclusion Regional impact HSG Alumni HSG Foundation Offers for the public Offers for the public Overview Public Lectures Children’s University HSG SQUARE Experiencing the HSG Info Desk and contact Library Library Overview Search and Use Research and publishing Visiting and Studying Contact and Consultation Schools Schools Overview School of Computer Science School of Economics and Political Science School of Finance School of Humanities and Social Sciences Law School School of Management Working at HSG Working at HSG Overview Jobs Working in administration Working in Academia Apprenticeship at HSG Life in Switzerland Entry from abroad: First steps Great Career Opportunities home more_horiz Studying Studying Research Executive Education Transfer News University Why HSG? Why HSG? Programmes Exchange programmes Get in touch Admissions Studying at HSG Orientation Great career opportunities Engaged community Great career opportunities Superb study programmes HSG Best Talents Four out of five bachelor’s and master’s graduates have at least one job offer by the time they graduate. A University of St.Gallen (HSG) qualification is recognised internationally as an indicator of high quality and, as a result, you are likely to receive multiple offers as you look to start your career. Alternatively, you may prefer to set up your own company – HSG graduates create a higher than average number of start-ups, most of them with international impact. You've Graduated: What Next? Master in Business Innovation (MBI) MBI graduates usually work in fields relating to the digitalisation of the value chain. One example is Kaltrina Abdili, M.A. HSG 2019, International Product Manager at ROCHE. Read more Master in Strategy and International Management (SIM) SIM graduates usually establish close contacts with leading organisations during their studies, like Kirsimarja Säkkinen, M.A. HSG 2020: Partner Development Manager at MICROSOFT. Read more Master in General Management (MGM) MGM graduates usually take on management roles in major groups, medium-sized companies or start-ups, just like Dr Tobias Wolf and Dr Philipp Wustrow, M.A. HSG 2014, Co-founders and Co-CEOs at ONLINEDOCTOR. Read more Master in International Affairs and Governance (MIA) MIA graduates usually work for international companies, in the diplomatic service or for NGOs. A good example is Simeon Bond, M.A. HSG 2021, Communication and Outreach Officer at the ILO (International Labour Organization). Read more Master in International Law (MIL) MIL graduates usually work in government, international organisations or management consultancies, like Ryan Humbert, M.A. HSG 2018, Project Manager at REFUGEES YOUTH SERVICE. Read more Master in Legal Studies and Economic Sciences (MLE) MLE graduates usually work as attorneys in Switzerland or at the interface between law and economics, like Kerim Tbaishat, B.A. HSG 2014 and M.A. HSG 2017, Attorney at BÄR & KARRER. Read more 1 / 6 Employability Facts 372 companies recruit at HSG every year. 79 % of HSG bachelor’s graduates have more than six months of professional/practical experience. 95 % of HSG master’s graduates have more than six months of professional/practical experience. 81 % of HSG bachelor’s graduates have a permanent position at the time of their graduation ceremony and can choose from an average of 1.8 job offers. 86 % of HSG master’s graduates have a permanent position at the time of their graduation ceremony and can choose from an average of 1.7 job offers. Career Centre Start your career with the right guidance east Find out more Your Launchpad For Launching a Business Discover how HSG supports founders east Find out more Why HSG? east Engaged Community east Superb Study Programmes east north From insight to impact. Search Search search Social Media University of St.Gallen Info Desk Contact and location map Library Media Advisory offices Intranet (Login) Emergency Contact University of St.Gallen Dufourstrasse 50 9000 St.Gallen Switzerland Accreditations Member of © Copyright 2026 University of St.Gallen, Switzerland Copyright & Disclaimer Data Protection Declaration Privacy settings"
    },
    "https://www.unisg.ch/en/research/faculty/open-faculty-positions/": {
      "title": "Open Faculty Positions",
      "description": "HSG - Uni SG - Open Faculty Positions Privacy settings We use cookies/targeting and process personal data to measure results and/or tailor the content of our website. Because we value your privacy, we ask for your permission. You can change/adjust your consent at any time in the \"Privacy settings\". Accept all cookies Accept required cookies Settings Data Protection Declaration Copyright & Disclaimer Privacy settings × Required cookies TYPO3 Consent Management Solution Functional cookies and pixels Google Analytics Crazy Egg Marketing cookies and pixels LinkedIn Meta Pixel Google Ads / Google Marketing Platform TikTok Pinterest Reddit Application related cookies Vimeo Youtube iFrame Other Applications Google Maps Required cookies This concerns: this consent menu incl. proof of consent TYPO3-Session Cookie (file transferred to the user's computer). Cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be deactivated. However, you can set your browser to block these cookies or to notify you of these cookies. However, some areas of the website will then not function or only function to a limited extent. For further information, please refer to the HSG data protection declaration of the: HSG – Website HSG – Your information request and voluntary contributions TYPO3 TYPO3 uses so-called session cookies (\"cookies\") by default. A TYPO3 cookie is a small data file that is transferred to the visitor's computer, but cannot identify the visitor personally. It only stores the browser installed on the visitor's computer, the visitor's activities, and the user's name and e-mail address when the user fills out a comment form. Consent Management Solution When you visit the website, \"cookies\" may be installed on your computer's hard drive for the sole purpose of making the website more responsive to the needs of returning visitors. These mini-files or cookies are not used to monitor the visitor's browsing behaviour on other websites. Internet browsers allow you to block the use of cookies. You will receive a warning when a cookie is installed or a notification that the cookies can then be removed from your hard drive. Please refer to the help function of your internet browser. Functional cookies and pixels These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They are set by third-party providers whose services the HSG uses on the pages of its domain. For further information, please refer to the HSG data protection declaration of the: HSG – Third Parties Google Analytics Google Analytics is a web analytics service provided by Alphabet Inc / Google LLC / Google Ireland Limited / Google Inc for the purpose of analysing how users use the website. Specifically: Reporting on website activity for the HSG Provision of other services associated with the use of the website and the Internet. After the cookie has been saved on your computer, personal data is collected: IP address / abbreviated IP address Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://policies.google.com/privacy Information on the third party can be found at: about.google Crazy Egg Crazy Egg is a website optimisation tool to obtain statistics about user behaviour on a website. Once the cookie is stored on your computer, it can help optimise the website for your use. In-formation is stored which provides information about where you have clicked: where you clicked how long you stayed on individual pages of the domain The following are transmitted to Crazy Egg: the first three bytes of your IP address the click coordinates other parameters provided by your web browser Information on data protection, retention period, storage locations and third parties can be found at: www.crazyegg.com/ Marketing cookies and pixels These cookies may be set by advertising partners. They may be used by these companies to profile your interests and show you relevant ads on other websites. This is based on a unique identification of your browser and internet device. For further information, please refer to the HSG data protection declaration of the: HSG – Third Parties LinkedIn It is used by LinkedIn Corporation: Conversion tracking technology Retargeting function This technology can be used to serve personalised ads on LinkedIn to users of this website. Furthermore, it is possible to create anonymous reports on the performance of the advertise-ments and information on website interaction. For this purpose, the LinkedIn In-Sight tag is integrated on this website, which establishes a connection to the LinkedIn server if you are logged into your LinkedIn account at the same time. Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://www.linkedin.com/legal/privacy-policy Information on the third party can be found at: https://www.linkedin.com Meta Pixel This is a tracking technology of Facebook Inc. / Facebook Ireland Limited, which is placed as a pixel in the browser and used for: Marketing Retargeting Tracking Analysis Advertising The following personal data is collected: Facebook user ID Browser information Usage data Non-sensitive custom data Referrer URL Pixel ID User behaviour Advertisements viewed Interactions with advertisements, services and products Marketing information Viewed content IP address Device information Marketing campaign success Geographical location Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://www.facebook.com/privacy/explanation Information on the third party can be found at: https://www.facebook.com Google Ads / Google Marketing Platform It is a service of Alphabet Inc. / Google LLC / Google Ireland Limited / Google Inc. for the pur pose of internet advertising, which allows advertisers to place ads in Google's search engine results as well as in the Google advertising network. The purpose of Google Ads / Google Marketing Platforms is the insertion of interest-relevant advertising on the websites of third-party companies and in the search engine results of the Google search engine, as well as the insertion of third-party advertising. A so-called conversion cookie is stored by Google in the information technology system of the data subject. In connection with AdWords and personal data, such as an IP address, Google: understands whether a data subject has completed or cancelled a purchase of goods compiles visit statistics determines the success or failure of AdWords ads and optimizes them Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://www.google.de/intl/de/policies/privacy/ Information on the third party can be found at: https://about.google/ TikTok This is a code from TikTok Information Technologies UK Limited which is implemented as a pixel on the website for the purpose of displaying targeted and personalised advertising to us-ers and to create interest-based user profiles. A connection is established to TikTok servers to collect the following personal data: IP address E-mail address Unit ID Device type Operating System In addition, behaviour on websites can be tracked, e.g. for measuring the effectiveness of ad placements. Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://www.tiktok.com/legal/page/eea/new-privacy-policy/en-EN Information on the third party can be found at: https://www.tiktok.com/ Pinterest Pinterest is a service provided by Pinterest Inc., USA, which is integrated into the website as a pixel, widget, or pin button for marketing and analysis purposes relating to users. A connection is established to Pinterest servers in order to collect the following personal data: Technical data: IP address Device information Browser information Operating system Screen resolution Language settings Usage data: Date/time of access Pages viewed Referrer URL (e.g., coming from Pinterest) Click behavior Cookie/tracking data: Unique Ids Session Ids Possibly hashed email address (if known) Location data (derived from IP or device information) Interaction data (content that is shared, pinned, or clicked on) Information on data protection, retention periods, and storage locations, including the US, can be found at: https://policy.pinterest.com/en/privacy-policy Reddit Functions of the Reddit platform are integrated into the website (the so-called Reddit Pixel). The provider is: Reddit Inc., 548 Market St #16093, San Francisco, CA 94104, USA. Reddit is a service provided by Reddit company, which is embedded as a pixel on the website of the University of St.Gallen. To optimise our content for your needs, personal and behavioural data are collected and processed in analytics tools such as Google Analytics, in particular: IP address Browser and device data Date and time of access Referrer URL (our website) Information about your use of embedded content Existing Reddit cookies or tracking IDs Reddit may use these data to provide embedded content, analyse user behaviour, display personalised content or advertising, and ensure the security of the platform. Further information about the purpose and scope of data collection by Reddit, the storage period and the storage locations in the United States can be found at: Reddit Privacy Policy Application related cookies These cookies are required by third party regulations when users voluntarily apply the relevant element. For further information, please refer to the HSG data protection declaration of the: HSG – Third Parties Vimeo This is a service provided by Vimeo LLC for the purpose of displaying video content. A cookie is placed in the browser and used to collect the following personal data: Browser information Browser language Browser type Cookie information Device information Device operating system Information from third party sources IP address Pages visited Referring URL Information users provide on the website Search queries Geographical location Retrieved content Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://vimeo.com/privacy Information on the third party can be found at: https://vimeo.com/ Youtube This is a service provided by Alphabet Inc. / Google LLC / Google Ireland Limited / Google Inc. for the purpose of displaying video content. A cookie is placed in the browser if the privacy-friendly mode is not activated and is used to collect the following personal data: Device information IP address Referring URL Retrieved videos Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=en Information on the third party can be found at: https://about.google/ iFrame Fremde Inhalte können per iFrame in der Seite integriert sein. Other Applications For further information, please refer to the HSG data protection declaration of the: HSG – Third Parties Google Maps This is an API (\"Application Programming Interface\") for the map service of Alphabet Inc. / Google LLC / Google Ireland Limited / Google Inc. for the purpose of an appealing presentation of the online offer and an easy findability of specified locations. When used, the IP address is collected as a personal data. No cookies are used. Information on data protection, retention period and storage locations can be found at: https://www.google.com/intl/de_de/help/terms_maps/ Information on the third party can be found at: https://about.google/ Cancel Save and close path d=\"m521.23-480-123 123L440-314.23 605.77-480 440-645.77 398.23-603l123 123Zm-41.16 380q-78.84 0-148.21-29.92t-120.68-81.21q-51.31-51.29-81.25-120.63Q100-401.1 100-479.93q0-78.84 29.92-148.21t81.21-120.68q51.29-51.31 120.63-81.25Q401.1-860 479.93-860q78.84 0 148.21 29.92t120.68 81.21q51.31 51.29 81.25 120.63Q860-558.9 860-480.07q0 78.84-29.92 148.21t-81.21 120.68q-51.29 51.31-120.63 81.25Q558.9-100 480.07-100Zm-.07-60q134 0 227-93t93-227q0-134-93-227t-227-93q-