ing and Studying Contact and Consultation Schools Schools Overview School of Computer Science School of Economics and Political Science School of Finance School of Humanities and Social Sciences Law School School of Management Working at HSG Working at HSG Overview Jobs Working in administration Working in Academia Apprenticeship at HSG Life in Switzerland Entry from abroad: First steps Academic Career Development home more_horiz Research Studying Research Executive Education Transfer News University Ph.D. Research at HSG Faculty Research units Ph.D. Research in Focus Alexandria Early Career Programme PhD Programme in Management (PMA) Graduate Programme in Economics and Finance (GPEF) Computer Science (DCS) Law (DLS) Organization Studies and Cultural Theory (DOK) International Affairs and Political Economy (DIA) Early Career Programme Academic Career Development With our transferable skills trainings we are committed to support early career researchers in developing interdisciplinary competencies. The Academic Career Development offers trainings, workshops and many resources that offer skills and guidance given your current qualification level. Our offers are designed to ensure that you are well integrated into the academic system and acquire skills that will enable you to complete your dissertation successfully and effectively. Are you considering a career in academia? We offer support to sharpen your academic profile and to develop competencies relevant to prepare you for appointment procedures. For more information please refer to our Mid-Career Programme. Workshops and Trainings east Workshops Offers from our Network Partner east Offers Writing your Dissertation east Offers Starting your PhD Studies east Guidance The Research Stage east Research Stage PhD Office east PhD Office PhD in a Nutshell east Brochure (in German) PhD Programmes 2024 east PhD Programmes The PhD Journey: A Shared Responsiblity east PhD Journey Erfolgreich promovieren (in German) east Download file Promotion - und dann? (in German) east Download file What To Do in Case of Conflict east Download file Details Write e-mail Sarah Howlader Student Assistant Write e-mail Allgemeine Rahmenbedingungen (AGB, in German) 2302_AGB_ECP ― PDF, 182 KB save_alt north From insight to impact. Search Search search Social Media University of St.Gallen Info Desk Contact and location map Library Media Advisory offices Intranet (Login) Emergency Contact University of St.Gallen Dufourstrasse 50 9000 St.Gallen Switzerland Accreditations Member of © Copyright 2026 University of St.Gallen, Switzerland Copyright & Disclaimer Data Protection Declaration Privacy settings"
